{title: Greensleeves}
{artist: Traditional}
{key: Am}

{c: Verse 1}
A[Am]las, my [G]love, you [Am]do me [E]wrong,
to [Am]cast me [G]off dis[E]courteous[Am]ly.
And [Am]I have [G]loved you [Am]so [E]long,
de[Am]lighting [E]in your [Am]compan[Am]y.

{c: Chorus}
[C]Greensleeves was [G]all my joy,
[Am]Greensleeves was [E]my delight.
[C]Greensleeves was my [G]heart of gold,
and [Am]who but my [E]lady [Am]Greensleeves.
